<title>AUSTRALIA: The Broken Hill Pty budgetting at exchange rate of US$0.78.</title>
<headline>The Broken Hill Pty budgetting at exchange rate of US$0.78.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Monday it was budgetting for an Australian dollar exchange rate of US$0.7800 in the year ending May 31, 1998.</p>
<p>BHP's general manager, finance, Graeme McGregor told a briefing seminar that for every one U.S. cent increase in the local exchange rate, BHP's after tax profit was cut by A$33 million.</p>
<p>The Australian dollar was trading around US$0.7455 on Monday morning.</p>
</text>
